  "id": "eval.2026-09-08-comp-134600.ivr-agent-handoff",
  "title": "Phone support with AI agent handoff",
  "description": "# Phone support with AI agent handoff\nRead the four bands from top to bottom. The call controller queries customer records before greeting, uses account context on a match or a generic greeting on failure/no match, captures recording/transcription consent, and collects intent by speech with keypad fallback.\n\nEligible routine intents go to the real-time AI voice agent, which uses read-only account facts and limited authorized actions. Ineligible intents or requests for a person go directly to the human queue; unresolved requests and low-confidence flags also escalate. Transfers carry transcript, account context, intent and completed work. Human availability is bounded by a wait target; otherwise a callback is offered.\n\nThe quality band represents call recording/transcription and review of unresolved or abandoned calls. Dashed violet feedback updates AI intent eligibility. Recording behavior when consent is declined remains a policy question.",
